From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:20:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: IMPLEMENT_ME throws in the native build.

Natively, a path DXMT has no code for throws std::logic_error after
logging, instead of aborting: a VM host's stubs catch it and fail the
call, so a game that reaches one doesn't take the VM down. The Windows
build still aborts.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/d3d12/d3d12_device.hpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d12/d3d12_device.hpp b/src/d3d12/d3d12_device.hpp
index 582366f..6fe9f82 100644
--- a/src/d3d12/d3d12_device.hpp
+++ b/src/d3d12/d3d12_device.hpp
@@ -34,10 +34,18 @@
 #include "log/log.hpp"
 #include "util_win32_compat.h"
 
+#ifdef _WIN32
+#define IMPLEMENT_ME_END abort();
+#else
+// MacNeutron, the native build: a VM host's stubs catch it and fail the call, rather than lose the VM.
+#include <stdexcept>
+#define IMPLEMENT_ME_END throw std::logic_error("not implemented");
+#endif
+
 #define IMPLEMENT_ME                                                                                                   \
   do {                                                                                                                 \
     Logger::err(str::format(__FILE__, ":", __FUNCTION__, "(", __LINE__, ") is not implemented."));                     \
-    abort();                                                                                                           \
+    IMPLEMENT_ME_END                                                                                                   \
     __builtin_unreachable();                                                                                           \
   } while (0);
 
